    client: "KFC",
    description: "Nuggets",
    overview:
      "Director Cloé Bailly of Iconoclast France was awarded the Campaign to direct four commercials—“Hot Dog,” “Crispy Naan,” “Double Tacos,” and “Nuggets”—for France and select neighbouring territories. The shoot took place in Cape Town, South Africa, where key crew members were flown in to support Cloé’s artistic vision. \n Iconoclast's line producer Vincent Véve brought on internationally acclaimed choreographer Supple Nam for the “Nuggets” commercial, where dance played a central role. Having worked with Vincent and Executive Producer Benoit Roques before, Supple also helped cast the lead role, conducting a search across Europe, South Africa, and the UK. Karl Magee emerged as the top choice after a rigorous selection process. \n Supple and Karl traveled from London for rehearsals, with Supple taking time to visit the location and collaborate with Cloé, who was already deep into filming the other spots. In a single intensive day, Supple crafted choreography tailored to Karl’s strengths, drawing out his full potential. \nThough Cloé had no prior dance experience, Supple guided her through the process, encouraging her to focus on directing while he handled the choreography. Despite limited time, Supple delivered a unique, quirky performance that bore his creative stamp and brought the “Nuggets” ad to life.",
