    overview:
      "Award winning director Sam Brown and Choreographer Supple Nam reunited to work on an exciting campaign for Lucozade, a double bill advert Bring the Energy. Basketball vs Northern Soul Dance and Football vs actors playing renovators featuring international football sensation Jude Bellingham.\nOn this advert Supple started by working out the strengths of the football players and football trickers, by creating conceptual exercises. He developed the exercises and ensured the footballers understood Supple's vision and ideas.\nBased on the treatment written by Sam Brown, Supple ambitiously choreographed in real time the 20 seconds of screen/edit sequence for director Sam, DP Harry Wheeler and 1st AD Ben Gill, to see. After breaking the choreography in sections, the team had a strong understanding of the intricate details. Supple and Sam flourished the choreography, developing the film and story. It enabled Sam the flexibility and freedom to best shoot the advert. Supple challenged the football players with skills to excite the concept to be more than just a football film.\nSadly Jude Bellingham had to postpone his appearance due to injury from a match. Which made Sam and Supple take alternative measures of not having the star in the advert.\nWeeks after this absent shoot with Jude Bellingham, a pick-up shoot was confirmed and put into place.\nSupple worked out the shots that needed to be picked up for Jude's appearance, keeping it authentic and true to the original choreography and concept.\nThe advert has been a hit since the release.",
