    description: "My Trigger",
    overview:
      "After the success and excitement of Miike Snow’s video “Genghis Khan”, directed by Ninian Doff and choreographed by Supple Nam (winning a D&AD award for best director and choreography). Both record label and artists management re-approached Ninian Doff to shoot the next Miike Snow video “My Trigger”, with talk of a sequel.\nNinian’s automatic request was to get Supple Nam on board, rattling his creative brain he finally presented a unique spin on “The Cuban Missile crisis”.\nSupple went into rehearsals with the 2 with the original lead actors from 'Ghengis Khan' Edward Hayes-Neary & Adam Jones to then bring in the 10 actors (non dancers), playing army generals to learn their section of the choreography.\nWith a 2 day shoot scheduled, Supple worked on and off set on both shoot days with his assistant to keep refining the choreography with the 10 actors. With the ambitious schedule, Supple and his assistant taught showgirl choreography to the 20 showgirls he cast, on the day of shoot.\nHonouring the anticipation of Miike Snow’s follow up music video to Genghis Khan, “Pull My Trigger” delivers yet another interesting and innovative dance routine.\n",
