    client: "Orange X Apple",
    description: "Rain Girl",
    overview:
      "French production company Diplomat Paris enlisted choreographer Supple Nam to collaborate with director duo Truman and Cooper (Anthony and Jonathan) on the Apple x Orange 2022 campaign for the advert `Rain Girl`. With a creative vision in place, Supple’s expertise was key in bringing the story to life through dynamic choreography.\nWith the lead role cast in London, played by 9-year-old Lacey Supple began working with her remotely through an introductory rehearsal on Zoom. After connecting virtually, they quickly transitioned to in-person rehearsals, where Supple designed and developed the choreography in close collaboration with Truman and Cooper, ensuring every movement aligned with the directors' vision.\nOnce the choreography was finalised and approved, Supple and Lacey flew to Bulgaria for the shoot.Upon arrival, Supple met with the directors, and they began fleshing out the storyboard as they discussed the location, the directors and Supple worked together to fine-tune the choreography, adjusting it to fit the space, camera angles, and story as it developed. The plot centers around a vibrant, imaginative young girl who wants to share her dreams and fantasies with her family—a story of creativity, joy, and the power of imagination.\nAs the shoot unfolded, Supple adapted the dance to align with the evolving story and shot predictions, ensuring the choreography was as dynamic and engaging as the narrative itself.\nDespite being her first commercial shoot, Lacey embraced the experience with enthusiasm and a positive attitude. Even in sub-zero conditions, her energy never wavered. Supple and 1st AD Mark Zarka worked closely with her, offering guidance and support to help her navigate the pressure of performing on camera for the first time.\nLacey's commitment, paired with Supple’s experience in coaching young talent, made for a smooth and joyful collaboration, resulting in a heartwarming and visually captivating ad.",
