    client: "Cisco",
    description: "Freeze",
    overview:
      "Choreographer Supple Nam Joins Forces with Director Thierry Poiraud for an Edgy, Iconic Ad.\nAfter a long break from commercials, French director Thierry Poiraud of Division Global returned to the world of advertising with a bold new project. Partnering once again with award winning choreographer Supple Nam in London, the duo was tasked with creating a commercial that was not just cool, but unexpected and fun—an edgy, unforgettable piece of work.\nBringing the Concept to Life:\nSupple was deeply involved in the casting process, reaching out to some of his top talents in his agency to find the perfect fit for the ad. Working alongside casting directors in both France and Lithuania, they selected Sharifa Butterfly from the UK, who perfectly embodied the character the team was aiming for. The client and Thierry were immediately on board with the choice.\nOnce the talent was secured, Supple began the intricate work of designing the dance to align with the concept. Every move had to be in sync with the characters’ motivations and the world they were inhabiting. Coming from the recce, Supple and 1st AD Amin went through each scene in a studio space, using props, mannequins, tape, and string to visualize and map out the obstacles and choreography that would drive the story forward.\nThierry was an active part of the rehearsal process, observing and jumping in when needed to refine the collaboration between film and choreography. The teamwork between Supple and Thierry was vital in crafting a seamless flow between movement and narrative.\nCollaboration at Every Step:\nGiven the complexity of the project, it was crucial for all departments to understand the choreography, which is why Amin played a key role in overseeing rehearsals and ensuring every team—from set design to lighting—was prepared for the shoot. This collaborative approach helped align all aspects of the production, allowing the creative vision to unfold effortlessly.\nA Global Hit\nThe result? An ad that went on to run globally for over three years, making waves in cinemas, on TV, and across the internet. Its success was a true testament to the creative chemistry between Supple Nam, Thierry Poiraud, and the entire production team. The commercial not only captivated audiences but also reinforced the importance of collaboration in bringing bold ideas to life.",
