    description: "Live Again",
    overview:
      "Chemical Brothers kicked off their forthcoming album for That Beautiful Feeling, with the music video Live Again, and designated duo director team Dom&Nic.On making ‘Live Again’, DOM&NIC said, “Working with the Chemical Brothers is always a dream for us. To have such a strong and inspiring piece of music and blank page to create a visual companion to it is as close to blissful creative freedom as it gets for directors.  This was our tenth collaboration with the Chems and we knew time would be tight on the back end of the project - https://www.televisual.com/  Dom&Nic and producer John Madsen approached award winning collaborators to join in this blissful project to make it special and help them achieve their direction on what this music video would become like.\nWe were showered with the generosity of such a strong and huge team of immensely talented companies and individuals that helped us to make this film happen because they love working with The Chemical Brothers. Many of them also worked with us on past Chemical Brother’s videos, it's become a creative family! Without their time, talents and generosity a film like this could never make it out of their heads and onto a screen. - https://www.promonews.tv/ \n One of the key collaborators was multi award winning choreographer Supple Nam, having worked with Dom&Nic many times he was excited to take advantage of this opportunity to develop his creative and working relationship with the duo.\nCasting with award winning casting director Thom Hammond, in search for the right talent that could match all their expectations to help visualise the video. The team reached out to talents all over the UK and Europe, where they stumbled upon dancer Josipa Kukor, with her selftape. Researching Josipa's background, the team invited her to a one to one workshop/casting session for Supple to see how she would work with him, where she was later confirmed.\n Supple insisted on inviting the duo to all his rehearsals with time and commitment to develop the idea. It was made very apparent how important it was to have the duo in Supple's creative space. Seeing and exploring thoughts and ideas, a technique was developed which became a crucial element in the making of the video. \nSupple's enthusiasm and passion transcended into Josipa's approach to be able to tackle the obstacles and challenges, all of which she took in her stride. The video started to see its story unveil and excite other collaborators as the wheel was definitely in motion with the Art department, styling, camera and visual effects. \nAfter 4 days of rehearsal Josipa stepped into the Arri Stage London studios on the prelight day, to walk through some technical steps.\nWith 2 days of shooting the project was all shot and ready for the post and edit. With technical glitches the whole company of collaborators took it in the stride with excitement knowing what they were all achieving was pushing boundaries.\nKukor delivers a brilliant performance, limbs stretched as far as they will go and a look of mischievous wonder on her face each time she steps out of her uncanny trailer. Whether she hitches a ride on a crane hook and scuttles beneath an alien spacecraft, the Croatian moves like a supple soundwave.\nThe result is a worthy companion to one of Dom&Nic's previous Chemical Brothers promos, 'Wide Open', with ballet dancer-turned-actor Sonoya Mizuno. If that film was cool and controlled science fiction, 'Live Again' is weird and wonderful fantasy. - https://www.davidreviews.com/ It's a trippy Groundhog-Day-esque adventure story through multiple environments in a continuous dance performance by the captivating and seemingly elastic dancer, Josipa Kukor.  - https://www.promonews.tv/ We were showered with the generosity of such a strong and huge team of immensely talented companies and individuals that helped us to make this film happen because they love working with The Chemical Brothers. Many of them  also worked with us on past Chemical Brother’s videos it’s become a creative family!  Without their time, talents and generosity a film like this could never make it out of heads and onto a screen. - https://www.promonews.tv/Live Again’ is a perfect Chemical Brothers track - unstoppable, resolutely hopeful and, once heard, utterly unshakable - it needed a suitably compelling video - https://www.lbbonline.com/ \nBritish Arrows Awards 2024 - Craft Gold winner for 'Innovative Use of Realtime-3D'.",
