    client: "Ikea",
    description: "Ghost",
    overview:
      "It became apparent that a choreographer/movement specialist would add value to award-winning director Dougal Wilson's Ikea advert Ghost. Supple could not pass the opportunity. Reading the treatment, he knew straight away what it would take to make this clever idea pop. Introducing his ideas to Dougal, he gathered a casting selection of an unexpected skill set of talents .\nTaking every opportunity from the casting, recall, fittings/rehearsals to add his flair to the concept “ghost” people under sheets, and execute it to the next level. Supple worked closely with Dougal during the prep to inspire him and share ideas.\nDuring the fitting, Supple and Dougal very quickly faced the challenge of the IKEA catalogue fabrics and rugs not falling correctly for the ghosts (people under sheets). Coming with solutions, Supple worked the obstacles into strengths by adding character traits where he could in the movement and over all performance. Safety and sight for the performers was another factor in everyone's mind. With ambitious ideas of people on segways, flips and break-dance stunts such as flares and windmills. Supple and production tackled all the problems to bring this simple idea to life and have vibrance. Working closely with the styling/costume department to add shape and protect the performers; helmets, bands for hands and legs were some of the techniques used.\nThe response to the final edit was everything everyone expected and more. Making it to cinema and all media platforms.",
