    overview:
      "Headhunted by Shine and Princess TV, artistic director and choreographer Supple Nam was asked to help develop a new TV dance show ‘Got To Dance’ (GTD) for SKY 1 and Sky 1 HD, a new platform for dancers to be stars of the show.\nWith Supple's experience involved on other dance TV shows such as Emmy Award winning So You Think You Can Dance in Australia and England, MTV dance reality show Bust A Move, as well as appearing on multiple episodes as a guest on Britain's Next Top Model to name a few. He wanted to bring a different format of dance on TV. The open minded executives in Shine and Princess TV, gave the opportunity to Supple to take the role.\nInjecting his ambitious drive, Supple's award winning experience on directing and choreographing live shows and film recorded dance performances gave an edge to the development of the show’s formula. Over seeing the quality of performance in the show, he hand-picked his team of choreographers to assist him. Quality control was very important to Supple as he supervised his team, as they mentored and trained all the contestants through to the finals. Spreading out on the home visits, rehearsals and working together on the live shows.\nAfter a successful first season, Supple was asked to continue with the role of Artistic Director & Choreographer for Seasons two and three.\nGot To Dance success made it to be UK & Ireland’s biggest reality TV dance talent show and was broadcasted live weekly, on Sky 1 HD. All episodes were filmed at the famous Pinewood Studios & in Seasons 2 and 3, the finals were filmed at London’s Olympia in front of 6000 people.\nSupple’s role entailed:\n– monitoring quality control throughout the entire talent process;\n– communicating with Executive Producers & Producers;\n– mentoring the talent;\n– choreography;\n– providing creative vision for camera setups (including: costumes, lighting, visuals, set design, music, props & camera direction); and\n– home visits to participating contestants.\nAired on Sky 1 and Sky 1 HD, the format’s host Davina McCall (Big Brother, Million Pound Drop) was joined by panel judges Ashley Banjo, Kimberly Wyatt and Adam Garcia.",
